# Documentation

[AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) is the navigation hub. Keep closer docs additive. Do not weaken security policy in prose.

## Accuracy

- Do not claim compliance, certification, exploitability, or remediation without describing the supporting evidence.
- Do not add aspirational features to MVP docs without labeling them as future work.
- Do not describe work as production-ready merely because tests pass.
- Separate observed facts from calculated conclusions.

## ADRs

- Lasting technical choices need an ADR using [docs/adr/template.md](../../docs/adr/template.md).
- Status values: Proposed, Accepted, Superseded, Rejected.
- Link superseded ADRs forward and back.

## Ops and security docs

- Significant features need an operational failure plan in a runbook when they are implemented.
- Vulnerability reporting stays in [SECURITY.md](../../SECURITY.md). Do not document exploit steps in public issues or READMEs.
- Keep internal Markdown links valid when files move.
